Failure Plan

| Failure | Safe behavior |
|---|---|
| Wi‑Fi or gateway disconnects | ESP32 continues local controls and energy rules |
| Bad sensor data | Mark data invalid and avoid automatic battery decisions |
| Battery data is stale | Do not assume battery is available; use grid fallback |
| Gateway restarts | ESP32 continues operating while gateway reconnects |
| Relay failure | Report mismatch through contactor feedback |
| Overload | Existing certified breaker stays primary protection; Wattch sheds nonessential loads |
| Power loss | Electrical protection remains independent; controller restarts safely |

Demo Data Flow

The Wokwi simulation feeds data through the real ESP32 control logic:

- The round potentiometer simulates household demand.
- The slide potentiometer simulates solar-panel output.
- The virtual clock starts during cheap overnight charging hours.
- Vacation Mode turns off AC/Eco, water-heater, and outlet circuits.
- Fridge/freezer, Wi‑Fi/security, and lights stay active.
- Raising simulated load above 15 amps trips the controller.
- The red LED and buzzer activate.
- Nonessential circuits shut down.
- Lowering load does not restore power by itself.
- A manual reset restores normal operation.
